lesson k-echoes v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=9 subject=music levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Echoes"
  goal "Copy a clapped or sung pattern exactly."

  look {
    scene 17x11 {
      beattrack b beats=4 target=[0, 1, 2, 3] played=[0, 1, 2, 3] tolerance=0.25 at=canvas(1, 1)
    }
    say """
        An echo copies exactly. The top dots are the claps to copy and the bottom dots are the echo.
        Every top dot has a partner underneath, so this echo is the same.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.echo-same m=0 level=medium
    }
    practice k.echo-same count=3 seed=2 easy-count=2 hard-count=2
    practice k.echo-count count=3 seed=3 easy-count=2
    show k.echo-clap
    show k.echo-sing
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.what-is-echo
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.echo-changed k=0 hard-k=1
  }
  remember {
    say "An echo copies exactly: the same claps, the same notes."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Clap and sing the patterns yourself; the page cannot make a sound. Clapping names read a rhythm
    from words; this is the step on from it, hearing a rhythm and copying it with nothing written.
    The clapped and sung echoes are for you to judge. If the child is stuck, make the pattern shorter
    and say it aloud as you clap. Off the page, play echo games on a walk with claps and stamps.
    England, Reception, ELG Being Imaginative and Expressive (recalled, not fetched): "Perform songs,
    rhymes, poems and stories with others, and (when appropriate) try to move in time with music".
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level a matching echo is worked in the teacher's pen first, the echoes to judge have one late clap or none, and the claps to count are few."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the echoes to judge have a late clap near the end, the claps to count pass five, and the changed beat is the first."
  }
}
